Off the top of my head, without having tried these in a speed run:

Digging down in Gehennom will save time, esp. if you'll be using c!GL to 
come back up.

Skip Sokoban, esp. if you already have a bag of holding or reflection. 
(worthless half the time then anyway)

Mine's end probably not worth your time. Definately hit minetown for the 
candles at least.

NO STASHES!!! Avoid backtracking, don't collect junk. The only place to 
leave equip is the entrance to the mines (you have to come back anyway). 
If you've got too much stuff on the way down, select some items you 
don't think you'll need until the end run and leave by the upstairs.


Probably the best thing you could do (in terms of sheer turn count): 
RIDE! A warhorse or unicorn has speed 24, a third faster than you even 
with speed boots (18). When riding them, your speed is their speed. I 
don't know if /oSpeed would add another 3 on top of that...

If you're going for pure speed, it's hard to beat someone riding. A 
ki-rin is another good choice, slower (18, aka 'very fast') but can fly 
and is more durable.

Thus, knights could do well for speed. Start with saddle, and no need 
for speed boots as soon as your pony (16) becomes a horse (20).


Before I get flamed, riding has some disadvantages. But if you want 
speed, you're gonna have to cut some corners.

